					<h1 class="title" title="Daman and Diu">Daman and Diu</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">
    
<p>Daman & Diu is the second smallest Union Territory of India, located on the west coast. It spreads to only 122 square kms. This coastal enclave has two districts- Diu and Daman.</p>

<p><b>Damanganga River</b> divides Daman into two parts; Moti Daman and the Nani Daman. This Union Territory falls near Gujarat so Gujarati influence is seen every where; even in the official language.</p>

<p>The island districts are the <b>perfect holiday destination</b> to people. The tranquility experienced amid the surrounding blue waters is a treat for the senses. You can take a dip in the waters, enjoy coconut juice just relaxing under palm trees or hover around the island to see the various tourist spots. In summers the temperature revolves around 17° - 38°C and in winters 10° - 34°C. So September to April is the <b>best time to visit Daman and Diu</b>.</p>
  
<h3>Places to see in Daman</h3>

<strong>Fort of Moti Daman</strong>
<p>The Colossal Fort of Moti Daman is polygonal in shape. Many official buildings like the Secretariat are located in the Northern side of the Fort.</p>
<strong>Fort of Nani Daman</strong>
<p>The small fort has three bastions and two gateways. The giant gateway faces the river with a large statue of St. Jerome and the gateway is protected by two giant human figures, one on either side. The <b>church of Our Lady of the Sea</b> within the Fort is an important structure in it. </p>
<strong>Nani Daman</strong>

<p>Gandhi Park near Nani Daman jetty, Lighthouse, church the Se Cathedral, Somnath Mahadev Temple in nearby Dabhel village and the fishing jetty in Nani Daman are places to see.</p>

<strong>Kadaiya Lake Garden</strong>

<p>It is one of the favourite man-made tourist destinations. The view of two islands connected via a bridge looks as like two eyes embedded on the face. The greenery, fountains and beautiful boats along with playful toy train adds upto its charm. </p>

<p>The Kadaiya Lake Garden is a famous tourist spot for shooting of many films. Mirasol Water Park in the garden is a perfect place to enjoy fun activities.</p>

<strong>Devka Beach</strong>
<p>The beautiful and well maintained amusement park with its musical fountain and kid's corner at <b>Devka beach</b> has always attracts the tourists.  Children enjoy pony - ride on the sands.</p>
<strong>Jampore Beach</strong>

<p><b>Jampore Beach</b> extends to Gujarat in the south. It is a place where you can romance with nature. The sea-shore is an ideal place for picnic. Strolling in wet sandy beach is an enthralling experience.</p>

<h3>Places to see in Diu</h3>

<strong>Nagoa Beach</strong>

<p><b>Nagoa Beach</b>  is the most popular semi-circular beach. The playful waves coming to the shores wheedle you to take a dip, play on the edges or engage in water sports. Quiet Gomptimata, Chakratirth near it are the other favorite beaches. </p>
 
<strong>Gangeshwar Temple</strong>

<p>Gangeshwar temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva. Five lingas present in the middle of rocks on the shore represent Shiva and are continuously rinsed by the sea waves.</p>
 
<strong>Ghoghla Beach</strong>

<p>Ghoghla Beach offers opportunities for water sports to tourists.</p>
 
<strong>St. Thomas Church and Museum</strong>

<p>St. Thomas's Church is now Diu Museum. The magnificent building is constructed in gothic architectural style. </p>
   
<strong>Diu Fort </strong>

<p>Diu Fort erected on the coast arrests the attention of everyone. The ancient stonework of the fort overwhelms you by its majesty. </p>


    
